00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.870 align:start position:0%
 
the work i've  done over the last 30 years since i left  the gsb has been very interesting  intersection of business and technology  and creativity  it's only after i left the business  school that i came to enjoy working with  technology and doing cool things with it  when i graduated there was a huge  recession and i kind of decided to go  the entrepreneurial route did one  startup doing control systems our focus  was on doing large concerts we had  clients like the grateful dead actually  so i graduated from stanford and a year  later i was on tour with a grateful dad  living in a tour bus  it really helped me learn how the  product work how the industry worked  learn the customers and it was  incredibly educational for my six weeks  of concert touring being a roadie we  sold that company and then saw a ted  video that i was really inspired by  these professors flying fleets of drones  in formation and i thought wow that'd be  really cool to do an entertainment so i  found  a group of young robotics engineers and  we joined forces  we spent three years developing the  technology and then have been flying  shows for the last two years  we make drones and the software needed  to have them all performed in a  coordinated manner to do all kinds of  interesting things in the sky  drones can make almost anything in the  sky they are 3d repositionable pixels  and so we are  developing an entire system both  hardware and software that makes it easy  to deploy these drones and have them do  what our clients want them to do  the entrepreneurial courses at stanford  gave me a really solid grounding in  terms of how to think about business  opportunities what's needed to get in  place in order to be successful how to  think long term how to think  strategically many of these lessons hold  true today and are really important as  you're figuring out how to grow a  business into something really  successful and lasting  where things have shifted for me lately  is normally i was behind the scenes and  because we are exploring new territory  with drones and pushing the envelope  we've been much more the creatives  ourselves that's why we just went on  america's got talent and it was a really  kind of crazy situation because i never  really  envisioned myself being on stage but  there i was and  we put on this really awesome  performance and it was different and  unusual to actually sort of be in front  of the camera and be the talent and to  be showcasing the work that we've been  working so hard on over the last five  years  [Applause]  so one of the things that they always  talked about at stanford during the  entrepreneurship classes is that there  is no single path and that entrepreneurs  come from all walks of life and there  are opportunities everywhere and  i think i have lived that 100 percent my  name is nils thorgesson i'm the ceo of  verge era  you

